<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="lc-ol-introduction">
  <title>Introduction</title>
  <section xml:id="lc-ol-learning-outcomes">
    <title>Learning Outcomes</title>
    <p>Learning outcomes describe the knowledge, understanding, skills and values students should be able to demonstrate.</p>
    <p>The Ordinary Level learning outcomes are presented in five course Parts, in syllabus order. Each Part starts with the complete learning outcomes.</p>
    <p>Across the five strands, students should be able to explore patterns, explain findings, justify conclusions, communicate mathematics clearly and apply suitable methods in familiar and unfamiliar situations.</p>
    <p><em>Source:</em> <url href="https://www.curriculumonline.ie/getmedia/f6f2e822-2b0c-461e-bcd4-dfcde6decc0c/SCSEC25_Maths_syllabus_examination-2015_English.pdf" visual="Leaving Certificate Mathematics Syllabus (for examination from 2015)"/>. The published syllabus remains the authority for mathematical notation and scope.</p>
  </section>

  <section xml:id="lc-examinations-external-candidates">
    <title>Examinations, Evidence and External Candidates</title>
    <p>Examination questions are one way of putting mathematical understanding and fluency to the test. They also demand careful reading, selecting an appropriate method, showing reasoning and managing time. Regular practice under realistic conditions can provide useful evidence of progress, but an examination grade is not the whole of mathematical proficiency.</p>
    <p>As of October 2026, an adult or another person who is not enrolled as a pupil of a recognised post-primary school may still seek entry to Leaving Certificate examinations as an <em>external candidate</em>, subject to the State Examinations Commission's conditions. Candidates must arrange the required permission from the relevant school principal and comply with the examination entry procedures. <url href="https://www.gov.ie/en/department-of-education/publications/state-examinations-2026/" visual="Department of Education: State Examinations information"/>.</p>
    <p>Under Senior Cycle Redevelopment, revised subjects are introducing Additional Assessment Components (AACs) alongside written examinations. Where coursework is required, teacher authentication and principal verification are important: privately completed coursework cannot automatically be accepted. External candidates should consult the <url href="https://www.examinations.ie/" visual="State Examinations Commission"/> for the arrangements applying to their subject and examination year. The rules can change as revised specifications are introduced.</p>
  </section>

